@title Harvest 2026: Summary for Farmers
@subtitle Marlow Valley Extension Service, from a survey of 214 farms completed 2026-10-10

# Harvest at a glance
kpi Farms surveyed | 214 | five counties
kpi Region rainfall | 601 mm | season average
kpi Best county | Calder | wettest and best yields

This summary covers 214 farms across five counties. Yields are in tonnes per hectare. Calder, the wettest county, had the best yield in every crop. Dunmore, the driest, had the lowest in every crop.

# Yields by county
data yields = county,Wheat,Corn,Soybeans,Barley; Alder,7.4,10.2,3.4,6.1; Brennan,6.8,9.1,3.1,5.7; Calder,8.1,11.4,3.7,6.6; Dunmore,5.9,8.3,2.8,4.9; Elmstead,7.7,10.8,3.5,6.3; Region average,7.2,10.0,3.3,5.9
table yields title="Yields by county, tonnes per hectare"

Wheat ran from 5.9 in Dunmore to 8.1 in Calder, a gap of 2.2 tonnes per hectare.

# Rainfall and yield
data rain = county,rainfall; Alder,612; Brennan,548; Calder,701; Dunmore,489; Elmstead,655
chart bar rain labels unit=mm title="Season rainfall by county"

The wettest county, Calder, had 701 mm of rain and the best yields. The driest, Dunmore, had 489 mm and the lowest. The survey shows this pattern across five counties, not its cause, so treat it as something to watch next season.
